                <head>No. 280.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Pendleton</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-13"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 13,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 219.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your dispatch No. 424, of
                    the 25th ultimo, I beg to inform you that the Department has learned with
                    satisfaction of the success of your efforts to secure a favorable modification
                    of the German laws regulating the importation of plants from the United States
                    into Germany.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. BAYARD.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
